invariant: INV-17
file: ct_wipe.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: ct_wipe calls memset by name instead of storing each byte and
  word through a volatile lvalue. Where the compiler sees that body at the
  call, as link-time optimization does, it knows the call stores zeros
  that nothing reads before the caller's frame ends, and deletes it, so
  every wipe at the end of a function is gone. Separately compiled,
  ct_wipe.c still wipes, so no vector notices. bin/poly1305_equiv_test
  compiles ct_wipe.c into the same unit as poly1305_vector_blocks and
  looks for the powers of r on the stack below the call.

--- old
    for (size_t i = 0; i < head; i++) {
        byte[i] = 0;
    }
--- new
    __builtin_memset(p, 0, n);
    return;
    for (size_t i = 0; i < head; i++) {
        byte[i] = 0;
    }
